cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ghost-Vision in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Ghost-Vision: camera-free motion and presence detection using WiFi Channel State Information on ESP32-S3"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kalantary"
    given-names: "M."
version: "4.0"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mkalantary/ghost-vision"
abstract: >-
  An open-source system that detects human motion and presence from WiFi
  Channel State Information (CSI), using four ESP32-S3 boards and one router
  to form 10 radio paths (16 directed measurements). It includes node
  firmware, a desktop console with calibration, persistence-checked and
  multi-path corroborated detection and approximate zone estimation, a simulation mode, and
  documentation of the system's physical limits and failed hypotheses.
keywords:
  - WiFi sensing
  - channel state information
  - CSI
  - ESP32-S3
  - presence detection
  - motion detection
  - device-free sensing
  - privacy
